# Convert, preview, cutover, rescrape

WordPress on the hosting IP is the source of truth. Never scrape public HTTPS on a host that already returns `x-source: kv` (that recopies stale static).

## Origin IPs and Workers

- Server 2 / Batches 1–7 live apex → `fleet-static-worker` + origin `174.136.29.214`
- Server 1 / new batches → `fleet-static-worker-server-1` + origin `165.140.157.43`
- Shared `HTML_FLEET` + `fleet-static-assets`. Keys `{host}:html:` / `{host}:asset:`. Preview keys `static.{domain}:…`
- Do not move B1–7 live apex onto server 1

## New convert (apex still WordPress)

1. Scrape WP via the correct origin IP into `HTML_FLEET` + R2
2. Attach `static.{domain}/*` only; QA vs live WP (26-check, eyeball)
3. After sign-off, cut over apex + www to the same fleet Worker
4. Inject `/form-validation.js` (origin WP never has the tag)
5. Proof: `200`, `x-source: kv`, `x-fleet-host`, `/form-validation.js` 200

Scripts: `fleet-static-preview\scripts\Invoke-PreviewStaticOnFleet.ps1` then `Invoke-CutoverApexToFleet.ps1 -IConfirmApexCutover`. Adam `/provision-originless` is preview-only and does not take an origin IP.

## Rescrape (already static)

`Invoke-WpOriginToFleet.ps1` with `--resolve` to the hosting IP. `-SkipRoutes` if apex is already fleet. HTML-only (`-SkipAssets`) when only HTML/popups changed; full HTML+R2 when theme/media changed. Re-inject form-validation after every HTML scrape.

## Edit loop

Rollback Worker routes to WordPress → edit on WP → rescrape → restore fleet routes → verify headers.

Stay-WordPress excludes are never converted. Usman injects form JS on remaining WordPress sites; we inject fleet/static sites through Cloudflare.
